---

<section id="constellations" class="page-shell section-pad scroll-mt-20 border-t border-[var(--line)]">
  <h2 class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-[var(--text)]">Constellation value, ranked</h2>
  <p class="mt-3 max-w-[65ch] text-[var(--muted)]">
    Not every constellation is worth your primogems. The tables below show the approximate damage gain of each
    constellation for popular carries, so you can see exactly where the breakpoints are before you pull.
    <span class="text-[var(--muted)]/70">Gains are community-sourced estimates for a typical end-game build — your exact
    number depends on your stats and team.</span>
  </p>

  <div class="mt-8 grid grid-cols-1 gap-5 md:grid-cols-2">
    {constellations.map((c) => (
      <div class="panel p-6">
        <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-3">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text)]">{c.name}</h3>
          <span class="shrink-0 text-xs font-medium text-gold-300">pull to {c.best}</span>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-[var(--muted)]">{c.note}</p>
        <div class="mt-4 overflow-hidden rounded-[10px] border border-[var(--line)]">
          <table class="w-full text-left text-sm">
            <tbody>
              {c.levels.map((lv) => (
                <tr class="border-b border-[var(--line)] last:border-b-0">
                  <td class="tnum w-12 px-3 py-2 font-medium text-[var(--text)]">{lv.l}</td>
                  <td class="tnum w-16 px-3 py-2 font-semibold text-dendro">{lv.gain}</td>
                  <td class="px-3 py-2 text-[var(--muted)]">{lv.desc}</td>
                </tr>
              ))}
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </div>
    ))}
  </div>

  <div class="panel mt-6 border-gold-400/40 bg-gold-400/5 p-6">
    <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gold-300">The rule of thumb</h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted)]">
      A new character almost always beats a constellation <em>unless</em> that constellation is a documented breakpoint.
      The breakpoints that actually matter are the ones that ignore DEF (Raiden C2, Ayaka C4), let reactions crit
      (Nahida C2), remove a core limitation (Hu Tao C1, Neuvillette C1), or speed up a stacking mechanic (Furina C2).
      Most C3, C4 and C5 constellations are small — verify before you spend.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
